2026-07-29T14:07:42.6168111Z # `--sdk-root alp-sdk` is passed explicitly, and that is a FINDING,
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6168612Z # not a preference. Run from the workspace topdir with `alp-sdk/`
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6169093Z # sitting right there, `tan init` still reports "alp-sdk root is
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6169535Z # unresolved" -- bootstrap records the SDK only at
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6169938Z # `.west/tan-workspace-sdk` (its own staleness marker,
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6170388Z # west_config.rs:133), never as the `.alp/sdk-path` pointer that
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6170879Z # resolution actually reads, and A5's global pointer is written only
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6171389Z # on a RELOCATION, which a clean parent never triggers. README's own
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6171903Z # flow passes `--sdk-root ./alp-sdk` to bootstrap, so this matches
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6172389Z # documented usage -- but the documented NEXT step does not resolve
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6172852Z # on its own. Tracked separately; drop this flag once it does.
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6173245Z "$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/target/debug/tan" init \
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6173604Z     --from-example peripheral-io/hello-world \
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6173949Z     --sdk-root alp-sdk \
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6174238Z     --name my-app --non-interactive
2026-07-29T14:07:42.6174683Z test -f my-app/board.yaml || { echo "::error::tan init wrote no board.yaml"; exit 1; }
